Subject: [PATCH] rp2040: boot_stage2: at25sf128a: run the flash at clk_sys / 2

Local patch of this workspace (zephyr/manifest/zephyr/patches.yml), not
meant for upstream.

The Arduino Nano RP2040 Connect's boot2 is boot2_at25sf128a.S, whose
default PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV of 4 runs the XIP clock at 31.25 MHz with
clk_sys at 125 MHz. hal_rpi_pico gives no way to pass the define to its
bootloader project, so change the default to 2 (62.5 MHz, as the Pico
SDK's boards use). The fast quad read (EBh) is rated for 108 MHz or more
by the AT25SF128A's data sheet.

diff --git a/src/rp2040/boot_stage2/boot2_at25sf128a.S b/src/rp2040/boot_stage2/boot2_at25sf128a.S
index 72f751e..caf9f03 100644
--- a/src/rp2040/boot_stage2/boot2_at25sf128a.S
+++ b/src/rp2040/boot_stage2/boot2_at25sf128a.S
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 // as aggressive as possible.
 
 #ifndef PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV
-#define PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV 4
+#define PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV 2
 #endif
 #if PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV & 1
 #error PICO_FLASH_SPI_CLKDIV must be even
